{
  "slug": "repoatlas",
  "name": "Repoatlas",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "AI-friendly knowledge-graph toolkit for codebases. Seven Claude/Copilot skills that survey, map, validate, and query single repos or multi-repo workspaces as markdown — no runtime, no lock-in.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **7 skills**.\n\n- **Skills** (7): `atlas-bootstrap-workspace` (Bootstrap a multi-repo workspace — survey every in-scope repo, generate per-repo atlases in two phases, write the workspace…), `atlas-generate-tree` (Write a complete atlas tree (ATLAS.md + .atlas/) for one repo from a confirmed domain-tag proposal), `atlas-identify-domains` (Propose 3–10 domain tags for a repo before atlas generation — kebab names, rationales, and per-tag feature-count estimates), `atlas-query` (Answer routing, impact-analysis, bug-triage, and cross-repo trace questions using one or more Repo Atlases without reading source code…), `atlas-refresh` (Incrementally update an existing atlas to reflect code changes since its last verification, including bridge changes (in atlas.workspace.md),…), `atlas-survey-repo` (Read-only reconnaissance of a repository before atlas generation — capture HEAD SHA, manifests, top-level layout, candidate domain tags,…), `atlas-validate` (Audit an existing Repo Atlas (single repo or workspace) — line budgets, required sections, alphabetical ordering, intra-repo and…)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install repoatlas@claude-community` from `SmallChX/repo-atlas`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "wrapper",
